{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795613454,"nonce":"BHK6EXUYaPyxSNCjSH1Sn+L4psg=","title":"A notch cannot be styled from a stylesheet, so the floating rich text toolbar cannot either","message":"`notch()` paints its fill, border and shadow from builder values. A rule on its class or id does not reach them. The rich text editor's floating toolbar is a notch, so its background, border, radius and shadow come from theme tokens in Rust, while the fixed toolbar takes `.blinc-rte-fixed-toolbar`.\n\nBoth toolbars must be stylable from CSS.","files":null}]}